Folio-OCR
=========

Third-party material in this repository, or fetched by it:

* folioocr/prompts.py: the doc2json and doc2md prompts are copied verbatim from
  the infinity_parser2 package (Infinity-Parser2, INF Technology), Apache
  License 2.0.

* folioocr/imaging.py: smart_resize re-implements the resizing rule of
  qwen-vl-utils (Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud), Apache License 2.0.

* folioocr/rl/teds.py implements TEDS (Zhong, ShafieiBavani and Jimeno Yepes,
  "Image-based table recognition", ECCV 2020) on top of the apted package
  (MIT License), which is installed separately.

* olmocr (Allen Institute for AI), Apache License 2.0: used as a dependency
  (installed separately, not shipped). Its unit-test classes score
  olmOCR-Bench-style tests, and its table parser reads tables for
  table-neighbour tests.

* folioocr/render/vocab.py and the page degradations in
  folioocr/render/degrade.py come from ResumeOCR-Lite (the author's own
  project).

* Fetched at setup by fetch_assets.py, not shipped: KaTeX (MIT License) and font
  families from google/fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, Apache License 2.0
  or Ubuntu Font Licence, per family). Each family's licence file is saved
  next to it under assets/fonts/.

* Models and datasets are downloaded by the user and keep their own licences.
  Infinity-Parser2-Flash is Apache-2.0. Chandra and Surya weights are not
  open-source licensed; this code only runs them as baselines, and their
  outputs must not be used as training data (label_teachers.py refuses them).
  Infinity-Doc2-5M is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (academic use only); olmOCR-mix and
  olmOCR-synthmix are ODC-BY; LightOnOCR-mix follows Common Crawl's and
  Digital Corpora's terms. folioocr/data/sources/common.py keeps one licence
  line per source, and make_data_card.py reports them.
